          "flavor": "Known waters. The charts don't lie."
        },
        {
          "event_type": "nothing",
          "message": "Incense drifts from a passing junk. In the East Indies, even the air is cultivated.",
          "hull_delta": 0,
          "provision_delta": 0,
          "silver_delta": 0,
          "crew_delta": 0,
          "speed_modifier": 1.0,
          "cargo_lost": [],
          "flavor": "[weather]"
        },
        {
          "event_type": "nothing",
          "message": "The light in the East Indies is different from anywhere else — softer, greener, filtered through atmospheric moisture that hasn't quite dried. It makes everything look like a painting of itself.",
          "hull_delta": 0,
          "provision_delta": 0,
          "silver_delta": 0,
          "crew_delta": 0,
          "speed_modifier": 1.0,
          "cargo_lost": [],
          "flavor": "[weather]"
        },
        {
          "event_type": "nothing",
          "message": "[bold]You arrive at Jade Port.[/bold]\n\nThe port is blooming. Literally — flowers on the docks, garlands on the warehouses, the scent of jasmine mixing with salt air. Spring arrivals in the East Indies feel like being invited to a celebration of survival.\n\nBamboo cranes lift crates padded with straw from the hold. Each piece of porcelain is inspected by guild markers before it leaves the dock.\n\n[bold]Harbor Director Li Wei:[/bold] \"Welcome to Jade Port. Your vessel will be berthed according to protocol. May I inquire about the nature of your cargo?\"\n\n[dim]Landmark: The Porcelain Quarter — a district of workshops where master potters fire kilns day and night.[/dim]\n[dim]Custom: Porcelain is presented on silk, never bare-handed. Fingerprints on porcelain void a sale.[/dim]",
          "hull_delta": 0,
          "provision_delta": 0,
          "silver_delta": 0,
          "crew_delta": 0,
          "speed_modifier": 1.0,
          "cargo_lost": [],
          "flavor": "[arrival]"
        }
